# Incident Response Analysis (NIST CSF Framework)

## Executive Summary
This report applies the NIST Cybersecurity Framework to analyze and respond to a detected security incident. The approach ensures structured handling across the five CSF functions — Identify, Protect, Detect, Respond, and Recover — to minimize impact and strengthen resilience.

### Identify
Critical assets and vulnerabilities were catalogued. The affected system was [insert system name], compromised through [insert vector].

### Protect
Preventive controls such as access restrictions, patch management, and firewall rules were reviewed and reinforced.

### Detect
Anomalous network traffic was detected via IDS alerts and tcpdump captures, confirming unauthorized access attempts.

### Respond
Immediate containment actions included isolating the host, performing forensic analysis, and disabling compromised accounts.

### Recover
Systems were restored from clean backups. Lessons learned were documented, and monitoring was enhanced to prevent recurrence.
